<title>UK: Brown cuts UK VAT on fuel to 5 pct from September.</title>
<headline>Brown cuts UK VAT on fuel to 5 pct from September.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown confirmed on Wednesday that he would cut VAT on heating fuel to five percent from eight.</p>
<p>&quot;I would like to abolish VAT on fuel. But European rules prevent me doing so. Therefore, VAT will be cut to the lowest level compatible with European law, that is five percent from September 1, well in advance of winter fuel bills,&quot; Brown told parliament in his budget speech.</p>
